{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg --files cores/bench/test cores/bench/sim_build -g '*.xml'; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/test/test_decoder_runner.result.xml\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen_runner.result.xml\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file_runner.result.xml\ncores/bench/test/test_div_unit_runner.result.xml\ncores/bench/test/test_alu_runner.result.xml\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline_runner.result.xml\n# Implementation\n\nImplemented the hypothesis in the five proposed RTL files. IF exposes raw\nimem_data throughout redirects and instruction-bus stalls; validity still\nsuppresses acceptance. ID keeps its raw decoded view but captures an all-zero\nID/EX bubble when an invalid fetch advances. The hazard unit now qualifies\nload-use detection with fetch validity. EX selects divider operands, operation\nand metadata using registered ID/EX occupancy instead of early_start, including\nthe existing EX/MEM-to-decode bypass when EX is empty.\n\nThe divider algorithm, four restoring steps per clock, eight-clock arithmetic\nschedule, launch/capture enables, result acceptance, pipeline stages, external\nports, single retirement channel and ALTOPS behavior are unchanged. No deviation\nfrom the hypothesis or evaluation-contract changes were needed.\n\nAdded directed pipeline tests for unaccepted raw DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU and load/store\nfetches, a rejected fetch matching an EX load destination, branch-flushed divides\nand memory operations, redirect during an instruction-bus stall, zero ID/EX\nbubbles, absence of false launch/interlock, and stale invalid forwarding metadata\nunder a held store. Tests check launch count and operand capture, early launches\nafter branches/JAL/load-use bubbles, zero destinations, both bus stalls, result\ncompletion while MEM is blocked, exact retirement sequence and exactly-once\nstores. Existing arithmetic, random-backpressure and retirement-gap assertions\nremain intact.\n\n# Local validation\n\n- Required Verilator lint command: pass, no warnings.\n- pytest -q cores/bench/test: all six simulator runners passed, including the\n  real ALU/divider arithmetic suites and the expanded pipeline suite.\n- RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh:\n  pass on the first attempt, 53 passed and zero failed. Includes ALTOPS arithmetic\n  routing, illegality, retirement uniqueness and bounded progress. No formal\n  counterexample or RTL fix retry was necessary.\n- NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench: pass; selftest RVFI comparison both with and\n  without bus stalls, plus canonical stalled CoreMark CRC validation.\n- Additional stalled CoreMark marker check: start cycle 15,801; stop cycle\n  4,507,286; measured interval 4,491,485 cycles, identical to the champion.\n  Completed with no out-of-bounds access; seedcrc=e9f5, crclist=e714,\n  crcmatrix=1fd7, crcstate=8e3a, crcfinal=fcaf and the validation literal present.\n- Vendor timing using python3 -m tools.eval.gowin bench --all-options:\n  placement options 0/1/2 yielded 45.687/44.180/44.180 MHz, median 44.180 MHz.\n  Logic 3,229; registers 600; LUT-RAM 40; BSRAM 4; DSP 6.\n  At unchanged cycles, median fitness is 98.3639 iterations/sec, a 19.8849%\n  Fmax increase over 36.852 MHz.\n- git diff --check: pass.\n\n# Remaining concern\n\nThe worst vendor path now stays inside div_unit's restoring recurrence and final\nsigned-result correction: 27.929 ns and 138 cells for placement options 1/2,\nfrom quotient_q_31_s1 to result_29_s0. The redirect/fetch/regfile launch path is\nno longer the reported limit. Real-arithmetic formal-deep was not run; the\nunchanged arithmetic is covered locally by the real divider vectors and cosim.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
