{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_67", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r13s0',\n 'title':'Flatten WB bypass and EX/MEM forwarding into one operand selector',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 220.50 iterations/sec at 92.886 MHz over 4,212,505 marker-bracketed cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. The history records failed carry-prediction and register-file reset experiments, while predecoding EX eligibility previously improved clock rate. The current register file applies an x0/WB/stored-word priority mux before forward_unit applies a second EX/MEM/register-file selector. This serial operand selection is unnecessary: the four authoritative sources can be selected together. Scratch timing reproduced the champion and found competing branch, divider and decode-forwarding paths, so shortening one branch comparator alone was insufficient. This proposal instead removes a real mux boundary from both decode operand buses without adding arithmetic, state, or execution cycles.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Flatten the existing register-file write-first bypass and decode forwarding into a single exact four-source masked-OR selection per operand. This is one local operand-mux optimization. Preserve the register file's storage, reset behavior, two asynchronous reads and synchronous write, and preserve every pipeline boundary, instruction latency, predictor and arithmetic handshake.\n\nAdd two raw stored-word outputs to reg_file, continuously driven by regs[rs1_addr] and regs[rs2_addr]. Keep its existing rs1_data/rs2_data outputs and their exact x0-then-WB-then-stored-word behavior for standalone compatibility and all existing tests. The core will feed the new raw outputs to forward_unit; its former bypassed outputs can be left internally unused and pruned by synthesis. Do not introduce a second physical register array, remove reset, or change write qualification. The raw outputs represent storage before the pending WB write; they must not include a WB-data mux or a read-data x0 mux.\n\nSupply forward_unit with the current wb_w_en, wb_w_addr and wb_w_data as a fourth candidate alongside current EX, MEM and raw storage. For each source address, calculate nonzero = source_addr \"'!= 0. Compute EX hit = nonzero AND ex_wen AND ex_rd == source_addr. Compute MEM hit with the same nonzero and matching enabled tag, excluding EX hit. Compute WB hit with nonzero and matching wb_w_en/wb_w_addr, excluding both older-priority hits. Compute storage hit = nonzero AND NOT(EX hit OR MEM hit OR WB hit). Resolve data as the OR of the four 32-bit candidates individually masked by their mutually exclusive hit bits. Calculate tag matches concurrently, then apply priority to their one-bit masks; avoid a four-deep priority data mux. Implement the same logic for rs2.\n\nThe priority must be EX > MEM > WB > stored RF, exactly matching today'\"'s composition of forward_unit and the register file. A source x0 activates no mask and returns zero even with poisoned storage or writes to x0. WB must win over the old stored value in the same cycle before the write edge. A younger EX writer must beat older MEM/WB writers to the same register. Preserve current producer enables and destination tags exactly, including completed MUL/DIV selection, trap suppression, load forwarding only when operand capture is permitted, and invalid bubbles. Do not add a readiness, redirect, reset or launch dependence to candidate data or tag selection. Existing hazard holds remain responsible for blocking admission of unavailable load data.\n\nRaw asynchronous RF visibility is harmless because only the masks authorize operand selection. Each admitted architectural operand, its ALU-input selection, store data and RVFI source value must equal the original two-layer network cycle by cycle, including stalled producer drain and result acceptance. No additional register, speculative result, replay, early arithmetic launch or change to fetch policy is part of this hypothesis.\n\nThe intended gain is removal of the serial RF write-first/x0 data mux before the decode forwarding mux, reducing LUT depth and routing on WB/storage-to-ID/EX paths. Estimate six percent higher fitness with low confidence: this exact candidate has not been vendor-measured, and EX forwarding, branch correction or divider paths may still determine Fmax. Do not claim the unsuccessful scratch arithmetic/branch variants as evidence of a gain for this proposal. At unchanged cycles, acceptance requires more than 230.643 iterations/sec, approximately 97.159 MHz median Gowin Fmax. Measure all scored placement options and unchanged marker-bracketed cycles; a smaller mux count alone is insufficient.\n\nKeep nret=1 and the entire core IO/RVFI contract, default-illegal decoding, all trap rules, exact real RV32M and ALTOPS results, strict retirement order, arbitrary memory backpressure, forward progress, memory bounds and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker invariants. Retain every existing correctness assertion and run standard formal, arithmetic tests, trace cosim, canonical CoreMark checks and median vendor timing. Scratch files are observations only and must not become build dependencies.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'Add two direct asynchronous stored-word read outputs while preserving the current storage array, bulk reset, write semantics and existing write-first/x0 outputs exactly. The new raw outputs bypass the WB and x0 data muxes and share the same read addresses and physical storage.'},\n {'file':'rtl/forward_unit.sv','description':'Add WB enable/tag/data inputs and replace the current three-source selector with exact mutually exclusive EX/MEM/WB/raw-storage masks and one four-input masked OR per operand. Preserve EX > MEM > WB > storage priority; qualify all masks with nonzero source addresses so x0 remains hardwired zero.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Connect raw register-file outputs to the operand resolver and wire the existing WB enable/address/data into its new inputs. Keep all producer qualification, decode capture, pipeline holds, bus ports, predictor, arithmetic units and RVFI unchanged.'},\n {'file':'test/test_forward_unit.py','description':'Check all source-priority conflicts against an independent model of the original forwarding-plus-write-first composition, both operands, x0 with poisoned raw data, disabled/stale producers, pending WB writes, matching destinations and randomized tags/data. Require exact source values with no added cycle.'},\n {'file':'test/test_reg_file.py','description':'Retain every existing storage/reset/x0/write-first assertion. Check that raw reads expose old stored data before a pending WB write and updated data after its edge, while the original outputs retain immediate bypass; cover repeated reset and writes to x0.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain current pipeline assertions and source/cycle checks. Add EX/MEM/WB same-destination conflicts, both-source consumers, WB-to-ID read-before-edge cases, x0, trapped/invalid producers, load-use and dmem holds, producer drain, arithmetic result acceptance and dependent stores/branches/JALR. Assert exact RVFI operands, order, side effects and unchanged latency.'}\n ]}\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r13s0.yaml')\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=92))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert type(h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Wrote final micro_opt hypothesis and validated schema:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
