{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_59", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r14s0',\n'title':'Remove synchronous reset from invalid ID/EX operand payload',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 220.50 iterations/sec at 92.886 MHz over 4,212,505 marker-bracketed cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Prior micro_opt attempts show that speculative carries, RF reset-validity changes and forwarding-mux flattening regress. Scratch timing reproduced the champion; arithmetic and comparator rewrites added routing cost or exposed the existing ALU-to-ID recurrence. The current id_stage synchronously zeros its entire ID/EX payload even though deterministic valid, ctrl and execution-eligibility bits already prevent invalid payload from affecting the architecture. This places reset selection and reset fanout on wide operand registers at the end of a timing-sensitive forwarding path. Removing that unnecessary payload reset is a distinct, smaller control mapping optimization; retain architectural register-file reset.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Separate ID/EX payload capture from the resettable instruction-eligibility state. Remove synchronous reset only from id_stage's raw payload fields: pc, direct_target, fallthrough_pc, predicted_transfer, recovery_pc, rs1_val, rs2_val, alu_a, alu_b, imm, rd, rs1_addr, rs2_addr and instr. Capture these fields whenever \"'!stall, independently of reset, flush and fetch validity; otherwise hold them. Their initial or retained values have no architectural meaning while the instruction is invalid. Keep the existing payload capture permission and pipeline boundary for every non-reset cycle, including payload holds on load-use flushes and backend waits. No combinational data path, instruction latency or execution schedule changes.\n\nIn the same clocked module, reset || flush || (!stall && !in.valid) must clear reg_q.valid, reg_q.ctrl, reg_q.fast_write, reg_q.mul_class and reg_q.div_class exactly as today. Reset has unconditional priority over a hold, and flush retains its existing priority over a hold. Otherwise capture these control fields on !stall and hold them on stall. Every side-effect authorization therefore resets deterministically even if a payload field retains an old value. Do not replace reset with an initialization file, initial block, FPGA-only power-up assumption or added valid bitmap. Do not relax tests to accept valid uninitialized instructions.\n\nThe architectural register file, fetch PC and skid validity, EX/MEM and MEM/WB reset behavior, retirement-order reset, branch predictor and MUL/DIV units retain their existing resets. In particular this is not the earlier register-file validity-reset experiment: x0, all architectural register values and write-first bypass retain their exact reset semantics. Preserve complete architectural operands on every valid admission, EX/MEM/RF forwarding priorities, all bus holds, correction isolation, default-illegal decoding, alignment traps, real and ALTOPS arithmetic, nret=1 IO/RVFI, strict order and bounded progress. Inactive ID/EX payload must never authorize a redirect, predictor update, arithmetic launch, register write, memory access or retirement.\n\nThe intended gain is removal of synchronous reset from the wide ID/EX payload capture logic and reduced reset fanout/routing, especially on ALU/forwarding-to-operand paths. Project six percent higher fitness with low confidence until all vendor placements are measured. The same ready sequence and unchanged instruction scheduling should preserve 4,212,505 marker-bracketed cycles. Acceptance requires more than 230.643 iterations/sec and approximately 97.159 MHz median Gowin Fmax. Competing branch and divider paths and Gowin'\"'s register mapping may limit the gain. Require ordinary formal, unchanged pipeline assertions, trace cosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker checks and all scored vendor placements. No evaluation-contract file or check may change.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Split raw ID/EX payload capture from control/valid reset. Clock payload fields only under \"'!stall without reset or flush qualification. Keep reset/flush/invalid-bubble clearing of valid, ctrl, fast_write, mul_class and div_class unconditional and preserve all non-reset admission and hold behavior. Change no other module'\"\\\\'s reset or datapath.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all architectural and bounded-progress assertions. Add mid-execution reset coverage with nonzero ID/EX operands, stalled decode, load-use flush, held older memory and pending arithmetic. Check reset clears all eligibility, architectural RF and order restart correctly, no stale payload executes, and the first post-reset valid instruction captures exact operands and metadata.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261004-001-r14s0'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Refined hypothesis written and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
