and ctrl.reg_write. Compute and register\nthe one-hot masks from those fields. After each edge, the chosen source\nmust equal the original combinational forwarding decision for the\nresulting pipeline state. Do not derive masks from an assumed normal\npipeline advance or simply hold an old selection throughout arithmetic\nwaits.\n\nMEM/WB forwarding intentionally uses ctrl.reg_write without valid:\nduring a data-memory stall it clears valid but retains its previous\nresult, destination and control for a held dependent EX instruction.\nPreserve that qualifi\n…[12693 of 15765 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c8d20866ce5785b6]…\npleted, retained exactly 4,773,913 marker-bracketed cycles\nfor ten iterations, matched all five CRCs and the required UART\nvalidation literal, and reported no out-of-bounds access. ALTOPS\nVerilator lint passed; complete formal remains an implementation\ngate and is not claimed here.\n\nAt the measured unchanged cycle count, that median projects approximately\n157.89 iterations/second, a 19.04-percent gain. Expect nineteen\npercent higher fitness with medium confidence. The main risks are\ngroup-zero negate-plus-3D timing, result correction feeding younger\ndecode/early launch, and exact preservation of signed corner cases\nand pending-result stability. Acceptance at unchanged cycles requires\nmedian Fmax above approximately 66.23 MHz. Preserve nret=1, all\nexternal ports, decode defaults, RVFI/order/trap rules, arbitrary\nbus waits, bounded progress and every evaluation invariant. Require\nexisting formal, real-arithmetic, trace cosim and canonical CoreMark\nCRC/UART/marker checks and reproduce the median vendor timing.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
