digit stages, each consuming the next two dividend bits from MSB\nto LSB. Each stage forms a 34-bit trial remainder T = 4*R + next_digit\nand computes T-D, T-2D and T-3D IN PARALLEL using 35-bit zero-extended\nsubtraction. Use the borrow bits to select the largest fitting multiple\nand append its two-bit quotient digit; retain the selected remainder for\nthe next stage. Derive the comparison from each subtraction's borrow,\nrather than putting a separate magnitude comparator before a subtractor.\nSelect mutually exclusive digit candidates with a shallow mux or masked OR;\navoid cascading three subtract-and-test operations within a stage.\nKeep wide trial arithmetic explicit to prevent overflow when D >= 2^31.\n\nObtain both the quotient and remainder from this same network. Apply sign\ncorrection to\n…[29556 of 32628 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ad1f0e49f44da09e]…\naps,\nmonotonic retirement, bounded progress and arbitrary bus backpressure.\nVerify old-versus-new early-launch equivalence, wrong-path DIV/REM on\nredirects and invalid fetches, load-to-divide forwarding, stalled older\nstores, result retention and exactly-once side effects. Require existing\nformal, arithmetic, trace cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker\nchecks and the unchanged median vendor timing evaluation.\n\nNOTES: \nhyp-20261004-002-r7s1 structural improvement fitness 174.53 MHz 83.321 cycles 4773913 critical {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_4_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -6.719, 'arrival_ns': 17.013, 'logic_cells': 9, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhyp-20261004-003-r7s2 predictor regression fitness 169.26 MHz 75.685 cycles 4471643 critical {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_negative_q_s0', 'slack_ns': -8.656, 'arrival_ns': 18.95, 'logic_cells': 40, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_predictor', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
