{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_82", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nclass Literal(str): pass\nyaml.SafeDumper.add_representer(Literal,lambda d,s:d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|'))\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r9s0',\n'title':'Capture complete fast-forwarding eligibility including jump alignment',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':Literal('''The champion scores 192.27 iterations/sec at median 91.790 MHz with\n4,773,913 measured CoreMark cycles. The previous winning micro_opt\ncaptured instruction classification and forwarding eligibility at ID/EX,\ngaining 10.16 percent. A fresh unchanged Gowin build reproduces 91.790 MHz\nand shows competing ALU-to-memory, EX-to-decode and divider paths.\nNo LESSONS.md exists. EX still puts dynamic misalign_fault qualification\nafter the captured fast_write flag. That qualification depends on branch\ncomparison and jump target calculation and feeds the decode operand masks.\nCapturing the complete eligibility predicate should shorten this feedback\npath without adding state or instruction cycles.\n'''),\n'hypothesis':Literal('''Retiming the remaining fast-forwarding fault qualification into the\nexisting ID/EX fast_write bit is one local Boolean/control optimization.\nUse the already resolved decode source operands and immediate to compute\njump alignment before admission, then let ordinary EX forwarding depend\nonly on in.valid and the captured complete fast_write predicate.\n\nIn id_stage add a two-bit combinational jump_target_low equal to\n(dec_is_jalr ? rs1_data[1:0] : in.pc[1:0]) + imm[1:0], modulo four.\nCompute jump_fault_decoded = dec_is_jump &&\n(dec_is_jalr ? jump_target_low[1] : |jump_target_low).\nJALR clears target bit zero, so only the summed bit one can misalign it;\nJAL requires both summed low bits zero. A two-bit sum exactly captures\nthe relevant bits of the existing 32-bit target calculation, including\ncarry from bit zero. Use final forwarded rs1_data, never raw RF data.\nAppend \"'!jump_fault_decoded to the existing decoded.fast_write expression.\nCapture this bit with the existing complete ID/EX payload, preserving\nreset/flush priority, all-zero invalid bubbles and every stall hold.\n\nIn ex_stage change ONLY the initial normal enable to\nforward_wen = in.valid && in.fast_write.\nPreserve the subsequent mul_valid/div_valid overrides and their priority,\ndata, destinations and eligibility. Keep the full existing misalign_branch,\nmisalign_jump, misalign_fault, ctrl_with_trap, redirect and pc_next logic.\nMisaligned branches and jumps must still trap, suppress redirect and\nsuppress architectural writes exactly as before. This precomputed flag\nonly authorizes the same normal forwarding candidate earlier.\n\nEquivalence follows from the existing decoder: conditional branches never\nhave reg_write, so their branch faults cannot coexist with original\nfast_write. JAL/JALR forwarding is excluded exactly by the captured low-bit\njump fault. All other fast writers retain their original eligibility;\nloads, M operations, illegal instructions and invalid bubbles remain\nexcluded. The source values used for this check are the same final values\ncaptured into ID/EX and remain stable when older producers drain during\nstalls. No new register bits, pipeline boundaries or execution cycles are\nintroduced. Keep the binary operation, arithmetic units and ALTOPS intact.\n\nScratch timing reproduced the champion. Full one-hot ALU retiming and\nshared-shifter arithmetic mappings reduced Fmax, and removing only branch\nfault qualification reached median 90.727 MHz, below 91.790. Therefore\nthis proposal removes the complete dynamic fault dependency at the\nexisting eligibility boundary rather than using those partial rewrites.\nEstimate an eight percent gain with low confidence: divider competition,\nnew decode timing and vendor mapping remain substantial uncertainties.\nAt unchanged cycles, the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold requires median\nFmax above approximately 96.012 MHz and fitness above 201.114 iter/sec.\nThese are targets, not a claim of measured improvement or acceptance.\n\nKeep nret=1, all external memory/RVFI ports, default-illegal decoding,\nstrict retirement order, exact captured operands, progress bounds and all\nmemory, CoreMark and stall invariants. Preserve every existing correctness\nassertion; update the internal fast_write expectation to include the exact\njump-alignment predicate while retaining cycle-level equivalence against\nthe original EX enable. Require formal, real arithmetic tests, trace\ncosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker/bounds checks and median Gowin\ntiming. Scratch files are evidence only and never implementation inputs.\n'\"'''),\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':Literal('''Compute exact two-bit JAL/JALR target alignment from final resolved rs1,\nPC and immediate before ID/EX admission. Add \"'!jump_fault_decoded to the\nexisting decoded.fast_write predicate. Preserve the entire register'\"'s\ncapture, reset, flush, invalid-bubble and hold behavior.\n''')},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':Literal('''Change only the initial ordinary forward_wen expression to\nin.valid && in.fast_write. Preserve full EX trap/redirect/next-PC logic,\nall data paths, M completion overrides, dispatch and handshake priority.\n''')},\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':Literal('''Update the existing fast_write field comment to describe complete\nnormal-forwarding eligibility, including captured jump alignment.\nChange no field width, order, bundle shape or operation encoding.\n''')},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':Literal('''Retain all assertions and retirement-gap bounds. Extend the internal\nfast_write reference with independently calculated JAL/JALR alignment\nusing captured PC, immediate and architectural rs1. Continue comparing\nactual EX forwarding against the original decoded eligibility AND full\nEX fault predicate. Add all four rs1/immediate low-bit combinations,\nJAL/JALR misalignment, link consumers, taken/untaken misaligned branches,\nx0, illegal encodings, producer bypasses and both bus stalls. Require\nexact operands/traps/order and no wrong-path retirement or side effect.\n''')}\n]}\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r9s0.yaml')\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Written and schema validated:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
