{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|register.file|forward|elastic|split|retim|pipeline' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Shorten combinational division with a shared radix-4 datapath\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 iter/sec at only 5.442 MHz. Its reported worst\\npath takes 199.837 ns through forwarding and the execute ALU, with 156\\ncells. alu.sv contains separate signed and unsigned divide and remainder\\nexpressions; their combinational division networks are the strongest\\ncandidate for this deep arithmetic path. There are no previous optimization\\nattempts or recorded lessons for bench. Shortening this datapath can improve\\nthe clock rate for every CoreMark instruction without adding execution cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 iter/sec at only 5.442 MHz. Its reported worst\\npath takes 199.837 ns through forwarding and the execute ALU, with 156\\ncells. alu.sv contains separate signed and unsigned divide and remainder\\nexpressions; their combinational division networks are the strongest\\ncandidate for this deep arithmetic path. There are no previous optimization\\nattempts or recorded lessons for bench. Shortening this datapath can improve\\nthe clock rate for every CoreMark instruction without adding execution cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operator expressions inside alu.sv with\\none explicitly unrolled, fully combinational unsigned radix-4 restoring\\ndivider, shared by all four operations. This is a local arithmetic mapping\\noptimization: keep the existing op/a/b/out interface and zero-cycle ALU\\nlatency, so the pipeline and its bus-stall behavior retain their timing.\\n\\nFor signed operations, form 32-bit unsigned operand magnitudes using\\ntwo's-complement negation; the magnitude of INT_MIN is 0x80000000.\\nPrecompute zero-extended D, 2D and 3D once at 34-bit width. Unroll sixteen\\nquotient-digit stages, each consuming the next two dividend bits from MSB\\nto LSB. Each stage forms a 34-bit trial remainder T = 4*R + next_digit\\nand computes T-D, T-2D and T-3D IN PARALLEL using 35-bit zero-ex\n…[310346 of 313418 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4852cbd13a777846]…\n explicit zero\\nvalid/ctrl/dispatch flags, absence of side effects, and independent\\npayload capture/hold assertions. Preserve all architectural checks\\nand test that raw-readiness load-use stalls equal the original\\ncondition whenever a real EX load can block an eligible fetch.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 200.29, \"delta_pct\": 4.17, \"vs_baseline\": 1552.56, \"fmax_mhz\": 89.562, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4471643, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4883, \"ff\": 1256, \"seeds\": [86.734, 89.562, 89.562], \"perturbations\": [[0, 86.734, 13], [1, 89.562, 11], [2, 89.562, 11]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_5_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -6.53, \"arrival_ns\": 16.824, \"logic_cells\": 38, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_predictor\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T18:30:03.501218Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
