{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(d['id'], d.get('category'), d.get('outcome'), 'fitness',d.get('fitness'), 'MHz',d.get('fmax_mhz'),'cycles',d.get('cycles'),d.get('title'))\n print(' path',d.get('critical_path'))\n if d.get('category')=='structural':\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(' PROPOSAL',h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print(' NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-0e2f75b micro_opt improvement fitness 12.12 MHz 5.442 cycles 4491485 Baseline retest for cores/bench\n path {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhyp-20261004-001-r1s0 micro_opt regression fitness 13.01 MHz 5.844 cycles 4491485 Shorten combinational division with a shared radix-4 datapath\n path {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -171.754, 'arrival_ns': 182.049, 'logic_cells': 496, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhyp-20261004-002-r1s1 structural improvement fitness 82.05 MHz 36.852 cycles 4491485 Replace combinational division with a bounded multicycle execute unit\n path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_1_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_q_14_s1', 'slack_ns': -24.323, 'arrival_ns': 34.618, 'logic_cells': 56, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_rf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}\n PROPOSAL Give DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU a shared, blocking multicycle execution\nunit, leaving the base integer ALU and existing multiplication datapaths\non their current single-cycle path. Remove all synthesizable / and %\nlogic from the core's instantiated ALU. The divider captures the actual\nforwarded source values once and computes unsigned magnitudes using\nfour explicitly unrolled restoring binary division steps per clock,\nwith quotient and remainder registered between groups. Eight groups\nproduce all 32 quotient bits. Capture operand magnitudes and sign flags\non the launch edge, and apply sign correction to the eighth group's\noutput when registering the completed result; do not add separate\npreparation or sign-correction states. This is four binary steps per\ncycle, not a large\ntable of trial multiples. Share the quotient/remainder state across all\nfour operations, use a widened trial remainder and subtraction borrow\nto choose each quotient bit, and regi\n…[48245 of 51317 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a11e3674651be174]…\npressure, arithmetic waits/completion, redirects,\nconsecutive memory operations, load-dependent addresses and traps.\n\nAt unchanged measured cycles the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold is\n201.11442 iterations/sec, requiring about 96.013 MHz median Fmax.\nProject a 10 percent fitness gain with medium confidence. Main risks\nare duplication/routing of the address adder, synthesis sharing and\na different critical path becoming limiting. This candidate has not\nbeen measured; require unchanged formal, real-arithmetic tests, full\ntrace cosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker/bounds validation and\nmedian Gowin timing before claiming an improvement.\n\n NOTES \nhyp-20261004-003-r9s2 predictor regression fitness 200.29 MHz 89.562 cycles 4471643 Agree prediction with recovery isolated from decode operand capture\n path {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/pc_5_s1', 'slack_ns': -6.53, 'arrival_ns': 16.824, 'logic_cells': 38, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_predictor', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
