{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"agent_message","text":"The full-width MUL paths reduced Fmax too much, even though they passed cosim and lowered cycle count. I’m now testing a narrower operand-dependent path: MUL uses one signed 16×16 DSP when both operands fit signed 16 bits, and retains the existing multicycle unit otherwise. This applies to any instruction stream and should cover many of CoreMark’s matrix multiplies."}}
