{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id') in ['hyp-20261004-002-r5s1','hyp-20261004-002-r6s1','hyp-20261004-001-r6s0','hyp-20261004-001-r5s0']:\n  print(d['id'],d['title'],d['outcome'],d['fitness'],d['fmax_mhz'])\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-001-r5s0 Register one-hot forwarding masks alongside pipeline next state regression 132.09 63.06\nRetiming the existing forwarding decision into six one-hot mask bits\nshould shorten the EX operand-to-result path without changing a single\ninstruction's execution latency. For each source, register a three-bit\nNONE/EX_MEM/MEM_WB mask on the same edge as the consumer and producer\npipeline entries it describes. Use NONE=3'b001, EX_MEM=3'b010 and\nMEM_WB=3'b100. Compute the mask from exact pipeline next-state tags and\ncontrols, retaining EX_MEM-over-MEM_WB priority and nonzero producer\ndestinations. In EX, select rs1 and rs2 with the bitwise OR of three\nindividually masked 32-bit candidates, rather than a binary selector\ncase. Reset both masks to NONE. This is one forwarding-control mapping\nand retiming optimization; keep ALU arithmetic, branch resolution,\nmultiplier/divider units and schedules, pipeline depth and fetch policy\nunchanged.\n\nExpress the existing ID/EX, EX/MEM and MEM/WB register updates as\nauthoritative combinational next-state bundles followed by clocked\ncapture. Preserve every reset, flush, hold, arithmetic-completion,\nbubble and trap priority exactly. Expose these next-state bundles\ninternally to the forwarding unit. ID/EX next state supplies source\naddresses; EX/MEM next state supplies rd and valid && ctrl.reg_write;\nMEM/WB next state supplies rd and ctrl.reg_write. Compute and register\nthe one-hot masks from those fields. After each edge, the chosen source\nmust equal the original combinational forwarding decision for the\nresulting pipeline state. Do not derive masks from an assumed normal\npipeline advance or simply hold an old selection throughout arithmetic\nwaits.\n\nMEM/WB forwarding intentionally uses ctrl.reg_write without valid:\nduring a data-memory stall it clears valid but retains its previous\nresult, destination and control for a held dependent EX instruction.\nPreserve that qualification exactly. A memory hold, load-use bubble,\nredirect flush, mul/div drain, captured arithmetic resul\n…[17624 of 20696 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8baa2b43c0edf2ef]…\nS, capture raw operands and operation at start,\nevaluate the four unchanged subtraction/XOR formulas during group zero,\nand return them on the identical eighth busy clock. Keep nret=1 and\nevery external IO/RVFI port, legality/trap check, retirement-order rule\nand fixed formal liveness depth. Preserve early launch after taken\ncontrol transfers and dependent loads and the at-most-ten-cycle\nready-bus retirement gap; changing latency is not part of this proposal.\n\nWith unchanged CoreMark cycles, acceptance requires median Fmax above\napproximately 66.231 MHz and fitness above 138.731 iterations/sec.\nExpect eleven percent higher fitness with medium confidence. Main risks\nare routing fifteen subtractors, first-group constant preparation and\nfinal sign correction. Use real arithmetic and pipeline tests plus the\nunchanged formal, trace cosim, CoreMark CRC/marker/UART and median Gowin\nevaluation. Scratch artifacts are evidence only and must not become\nbuild dependencies; recreate all logic in the permitted RTL files.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
