{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|forward|pipeline|register.file|bypass' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Shorten combinational division with a shared radix-4 datapath\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 iter/sec at only 5.442 MHz. Its reported worst\\npath takes 199.837 ns through forwarding and the execute ALU, with 156\\ncells. alu.sv contains separate signed and unsigned divide and remainder\\nexpressions; their combinational division networks are the strongest\\ncandidate for this deep arithmetic path. There are no previous optimization\\nattempts or recorded lessons for bench. Shortening this datapath can improve\\nthe clock rate for every CoreMark instruction without adding execution cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 iter/sec at only 5.442 MHz. Its reported worst\\npath takes 199.837 ns through forwarding and the execute ALU, with 156\\ncells. alu.sv contains separate signed and unsigned divide and remainder\\nexpressions; their combinational division networks are the strongest\\ncandidate for this deep arithmetic path. There are no previous optimization\\nattempts or recorded lessons for bench. Shortening this datapath can improve\\nthe clock rate for every CoreMark instruction without adding execution cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operator expressions inside alu.sv with\\none explicitly unrolled, fully combinational unsigned radix-4 restoring\\ndivider, shared by all four operations. This is a local arithmetic mapping\\noptimization: keep the existing op/a/b/out interface and zero-cycle ALU\\nlatency, so the pipeline and its bus-stall behavior retain their timing.\\n\\nFor signed operations, form 32-bit unsigned operand magnitudes using\\ntwo's-complement negation; the magnitude of INT_MIN is 0x80000000.\\nPrecompute zero-extended D, 2D and 3D once at 34-bit width. Unroll sixteen\\nquotient-digit stages, each consuming the next two dividend bits from MSB\\nto LSB. Each stage forms a 34-bit trial remainder T = 4*R + next_digit\\nand computes T-D, T-2D and T-3D IN PARALLEL using 35-bit zero-ex\n…[387687 of 390759 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7ba01dd2c92b9133]…\nct RVFI operands,\\nPC/order/traps, one producer retirement, no wrong memory request or\\narithmetic launch, exact MEM fallback and bounded ready-bus progress.\\nInclude both new RTL modules in the pipeline test source list and\\nadapt bundle unpacking without weakening any architectural assertion.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 182.8, \"delta_pct\": -10.4, \"vs_baseline\": 1408.25, \"fmax_mhz\": 81.761, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4472807, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5210, \"ff\": 1296, \"seeds\": [81.539, 81.761, 81.761], \"perturbations\": [[0, 81.539, 15], [1, 81.761, 15], [2, 81.761, 15]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_q_31_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_1_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -7.264, \"arrival_ns\": 17.558, \"logic_cells\": 21, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T20:03:42.268188Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
