a()+foff, filesz);\n            memcpy(dmem+vaddr, elf.data.data()+foff, filesz);\n        }\n    }\n\n29:static bool in_uart_range(uint32_t a) { return (a & 0xFFF00000u) == 0x10000000u; }\n35:// bench_cycles = stop - start, excluding init/CRC-printing overhead.\n67:    // --bench:  suppress per-retirement output; print only the final record.\n108:    // CoreMark's portme.c redirects ee_printf through this MMIO so the bench\n110:    std::string uart_buf;\n150:            // MMIO UART at 0x10000000: capture to uart_buf, don't route to dmem\n154:            // and exclude CoreMark init/CRC-printing from the timing window.\n162:            } else if (in_uart_range(addr)) {\n166:                        if (c) uart_buf.push_back(c);\n196:            snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf),\n257:        // Escape backslash/quote/newline in uart_buf for JSON string safety.\n259:        for (char c : uart_buf) {\n265:            // drop other non-printables silently\n267:        printf(\"{\\\"ebreak\\\":%s,\\\"maxcycles_hit\\\":%s,\\\"oob\\\":%s,\"\n269:               \"\\\"bench_bracketed\\\":%s,\\\"uart\\\":\\\"%s\\\"}\\n\",\nmake: Leaving directory '/srv/hwebench/tmp/89cd5fec/6752213a/r12s1-skid-probe/obj_dir'\n- V e r i l a t i o n   R e p o r t: Verilator 5.047 devel rev v5.046-331-g2cd9b8df6 (mod)\n- Verilator: Built from 0.870 MB sources in 17 modules, into 0.554 MB in 7 C++ files needing 0.002 MB\n- Verilator: Walltime 5.952 s (elab=0.007, cvt=0.045, bld=5.887); cpu 0.065 s on 1 threads; allocated 26.789 MB\nBuilt: /srv/hwebench/tmp/89cd5fec/6752213a/r12s1-skid-probe/obj_dir/cosim_sim\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
