{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_48", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r13s1.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-002-r13s1',\n'title':'Pipeline bytewise branch comparisons across the existing ID/EX boundary',\n'category':'structural',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 220.50 iterations/sec at median 92.886 MHz over\n4,212,505 marker-bracketed cycles. Its reported worst path begins at\nID/EX rs2_val and crosses branch resolution, predictor training and\ncorrection control. No LESSONS.md is present. Earlier deeper fetch\nqueues saved cycles but failed the acceptance gate; preserving the\nsuccessful single-entry skid buffer while shortening branch resolution\nis the stronger structural opportunity. A scratch registered-correction\nbypass preserved cycles and passed selftest/random cosim, but its first\nplacement fell to 81.431 MHz and retained the long training comparison\npath. It is excluded from this proposal.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Split architectural branch comparison across the EXISTING ID/EX\nregister boundary. Keep instruction latency, pipeline depth, direct\nprediction, correction timing, the single-entry fetch skid buffer and\nall arithmetic units unchanged. Decode already resolves complete source\noperands before this boundary. Compute four independent eight-bit\nunsigned less-than predicates and four eight-bit equality predicates\nfrom those resolved operands, and capture the eight bits alongside the\nsame instruction's operands. EX combines these registered fragments\nrather than comparing two full-width live operands.\n\nFor byte k in 0..3, define E[k]=(rs1[8*k+:8]==rs2[8*k+:8]) and\nL[k]=(rs1[8*k+:8]<rs2[8*k+:8]), using unsigned byte slices. EX forms\nequal = E3&E2&E1&E0 and unsigned_less = L3 | (E3&L2) |\n(E3&E2&L1) | (E3&E2&E1&L0). Signed_less is rs1[31] when the\nregistered operand signs differ, otherwise unsigned_less. Select\nBEQ/BNE from equal and its inverse, BLTU/BGEU from unsigned_less and\nits inverse, and BLT/BGE from signed_less and its inverse. Use shallow\nbalanced Boolean logic rather than a serial four-byte priority mux.\nEvery predicate is exact; there is no predicted comparison or replay.\n\nPlace the byte comparisons after the existing EX/MEM/RF operand\nresolver and before ID/EX capture. Preserve its producer priority and\nwrite-first WB bypass. The fragments must describe the same actual\narchitectural rs1/rs2 values captured for RVFI, including either raw\nsource field. Capture comparison bits with the ordinary payload enable,\nindependently of flush or fetched validity. Hold them with the payload\non load-use, data-memory and arithmetic waits. Reset deterministically.\nA control-only bubble may retain harmless comparison bits; existing\nvalid/control gating must prevent it from resolving or training.\n\nRemove the original full-width BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU comparison\ncone from EX branch resolution. Retain full architectural operand\nregisters for RVFI, store data, ALU, JALR and M-extension execution;\nonly conditional branch resolution consumes the captured fragments.\nKeep branch training's accepted-event qualification, folded index,\nagreement bias, queued update and stored-state lookup exact. Keep EX\nmisprediction direction, preselected recovery address, JALR full-width\naddition, misalignment traps, link-write suppression and authoritative\npc_next unchanged. No comparator retiming is proposed for SLT/SLTU.\n\nThis is one structural retiming of branch comparison, with eight\nadditional ID/EX payload bits and no additional pipeline stage or\nrecovery bubble. Its intended benefit is to move the wide comparison\nout of branch-to-fetch and branch-to-training paths, leaving only a\nsmall reduction after ID/EX. The tradeoff is an eight-bit comparison\nfollowing decode forwarding; an ALU-to-forwarding-to-fragment path,\nunchanged divider arithmetic or register-file routing can become the\nnew clock limit. Actual Gowin mapping must justify the change.\n\nProject eight percent higher fitness with medium confidence, pending\nmeasurement. Acceptance requires measured fitness above 230.643\niterations/sec, or median Fmax above 97.159 MHz if CoreMark retains\n4,212,505 cycles. Measure actual stalled cycles and all three vendor\nplacements; do not claim an improvement from logic depth alone. Keep\nnret=1 and every external IO/RVFI field, exact architectural operands,\nstrict retirement order, decoder-default illegality, full-width memory\nand target behavior, bounded accesses, real RV32M and exact ALTOPS.\nPreserve the unchanged ten-cycle ready-bus retirement-gap check,\nformal liveness/depths, all arithmetic assertions, full-trace cosim,\nand canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker checks.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Add four byte-equality and four unsigned-byte-less-than bits to\nid_ex_t, associated with its existing captured operand payload.\nDo not change downstream retirement bundles or top-level ports.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Form all eight exact comparison fragments in parallel from final\nrs1_data/rs2_data. Capture and hold them with the ordinary raw ID/EX\npayload, using the existing reset, stall and control-only flush\npriorities. Do not add flush/valid qualification to fragment data\nor its payload enable.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace only full-width conditional branch comparisons with exact\nBoolean reductions of registered byte fragments and captured signs.\nPreserve branch opcode selection, accepted redirect/training events,\ntrap handling, pc_next, forwarding, arithmetic and memory behavior.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain existing architectural/progress assertions and update internal\nbundle-layout extraction for the eight added bits. Check byte fragments\nagainst the exact captured architectural operands and branch outcomes.\nCover all six branch types, equal values, each most-significant unequal\nbyte, signed extrema, x0, EX/MEM/WB forwarding on either or both sources,\nload-use bubbles, arithmetic completion, both bus stalls, redirects,\nmisaligned targets and reset. Assert held fragments retain association,\ninvalid work has no effects, predictor trains once, and ready-bus\nretirement gaps remain within the existing ten-cycle bound.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated hypothesis validates:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
