ged divider arithmetic or register-file routing can become the\nnew clock limit. Actual Gowin mapping must justify the change.\n\nProject eight percent higher fitness with medium confidence, pending\nmeasurement. Acceptance requires measured fitness above 230.643\niterations/sec, or median Fmax above 97.159 MHz if CoreMark retains\n4,212,505 cycles. Measure actual stalled cycles and all three vendor\nplacements; do not claim an improvement from logic depth alone. Keep\nnret=1 and every external IO/RVFI field, exact architectural operands,\nstrict retirement order, decoder-default illegality, full-width memory\nand target behavior, bounded accesses, real RV32M and exact ALTOPS.\nPreserve the unchanged ten-cycle ready-bus retirement-gap check,\nformal liveness/depths, all arithmetic assertions, full-trace cosim,\nand canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker checks.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Add four byte-equality and four unsigned-byte-less-than bits to\nid_ex_t, associated with its existing captured operand payload.\nDo not change downstream retirement bundles or top-level ports.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Form all eight exact comparison fragments in parallel from final\nrs1_data/rs2_data. Capture and hold them with the ordinary raw ID/EX\npayload, using the existing reset, stall and control-only flush\npriorities. Do not add flush/valid qualification to fragment data\nor its payload enable.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace only full-width conditional branch comparisons with exact\nBoolean reductions of registered byte fragments and captured signs.\nPreserve branch opcode selection, accepted redirect/training events,\ntrap handling, pc_next, forwarding, arithmetic and memory behavior.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain existing architectural/progress assertions and update internal\nbundle-layout extrac