{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(d['id'],d.get('category'),d.get('outcome'),d.get('fitness'),d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('cycles'),d.get('title'))\n if d.get('category')=='structural':\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('  PROPOSAL:', h.get('hypothesis','')[:1700] if isinstance(h,dict) else str(h)[:1700])\n  print('  PATH:',d.get('critical_path'))\n  if d.get('error'):print('  ERROR:',d.get('error'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-0e2f75b micro_opt improvement 12.12 5.442 4491485 Baseline retest for cores/bench\nhyp-20261004-001-r1s0 micro_opt regression 13.01 5.844 4491485 Shorten combinational division with a shared radix-4 datapath\nhyp-20261004-002-r1s1 structural improvement 82.05 36.852 4491485 Replace combinational division with a bounded multicycle execute unit\n  PROPOSAL: Give DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU a shared, blocking multicycle execution\nunit, leaving the base integer ALU and existing multiplication datapaths\non their current single-cycle path. Remove all synthesizable / and %\nlogic from the core's instantiated ALU. The divider captures the actual\nforwarded source values once and computes unsigned magnitudes using\nfour explicitly unrolled restoring binary division steps per clock,\nwith quotient and remainder registered between groups. Eight groups\nproduce all 32 quotient bits. Capture operand magnitudes and sign flags\non the launch edge, and apply sign correction to the eighth group's\noutput when registering the completed result; do not add separate\npreparation or sign-correction states. This is four binary steps per\ncycle, not a large\ntable of trial multiples. Share the quotient/remainder state across all\nfour operations, use a widened trial remainder and subtraction borrow\nto choose each quotient bit, and register the completed signed result\nbefore it enters the normal EX/MEM result and bypass network.\n\nHold the divide instruction and younger work while the unit is busy,\nbut let older EX/MEM and MEM/WB instructions drain. Emit an invalid\nEX/MEM bubble once the older instruction advances; never retain and\nreissue an older store merely because the divider is busy. Keep data\nbus stalls distinct from divider stalls, preserve older WB values needed\nby a held instruction, suppress redirects from invalid entries, and\naccept the divider result into EX/MEM exactly once when MEM can advance.\nHold a completed result stable until accepted, without restarting the\noperation or retiring it twice. Resume normal EX/MEM forwarding\n…[27151 of 30223 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4e6d01d6e592a8f2]…\nulo 2^32.\nNo high-by-high product is needed for low-half MUL.\n\nIn MEM compute upper16=(P00[31:16]+P01[15:0]+P10[15:0]) mod 2^16\nwith a sixteen-bit carry-save compressor followed by one sixteen-bit\ncarry-propagate addition. The exact result is\n{upper16,P00[15:0]}. Capture it as the instruction's normal MEM/WB\nwriteback value and expose the same exact value on MEM forwarding.\nDo not append a 32-bit high-result adder or sign correction to this\nlane. Keep the full original raw operands in RVFI metadata.\n\nLow-half MUL has no EX forwarding candidate, just as a load has none.\nExtend the existing one-cycle load-use interlock to a valid EX low-half\nMUL with a nonzero destination \n  PATH: {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/pc_5_s1', 'slack_ns': -6.903, 'arrival_ns': 17.197, 'logic_cells': 38, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_predictor', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']}\nhyp-20261004-003-r13s2 predictor regression 207.3 87.325 4212505 Separate agree-predictor acceptance from late branch outcomes\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
