{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_48", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r14s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-002-r14s1\ntitle: \"Split branch comparison across the existing ID/EX register boundary\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 220.50 iterations/sec at 92.886 MHz over 4,212,505\n  bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path begins at registered\n  rs2 operands and runs through EX branch resolution into predictor event\n  acceptance; the latest structural experiment exposes the same source\n  through correction into fetch PC. Larger instruction queues and the\n  streamed low-half multiplier failed the acceptance threshold. Separating\n  predictor acceptance from direction alone also regressed. No LESSONS.md\n  exists. The remaining opportunity is to divide the actual 32-bit branch\n  comparison between existing stages, rather than only rearranging its\n  downstream control or adding a pipeline stage.\nhypothesis: |\n  Retime conditional-branch comparison across the existing ID/EX boundary\n  without changing instruction latency, branch prediction, recovery policy,\n  operand forwarding or arithmetic-unit scheduling. In ID, compute four\n  independent unsigned eight-bit less-than and equality summaries from the\n  final resolved rs1_data and rs2_data. Register these eight summary bits\n  alongside the exact architectural operands using the same payload capture\n  enable and hold behavior. Do not compute the complete 32-bit comparison\n  before ID/EX: the parallel local comparisons bound the extra depth on\n  EX-result-to-younger-ID and MEM-load-to-younger-ID paths.\n\n  Number groups from least significant zero to most significant three.\n  EX reconstructs EQ = E3 & E2 & E1 & E0 and unsigned LT = L3 |\n  (E3 & L2) | (E3 & E2 & L1) | (E3 & E2 & E1 & L0), with explicit parallel\n  product terms and a shallow OR reduction. Signed LT equals captured\n  rs1[31] when the captured signs differ, otherwise unsigned LT. Select\n  BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU from EQ, signed LT, unsigned LT and their\n  complements using the existing validated branch_op. Remove the original\n  full-width EX relational/equality comp\n…[2773 of 5845 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1d735c506f5dc0c5]…\n - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the six full-width branch comparisons with exact shallow\n      reduction of registered equality/less-than fragments and captured\n      sign bits. Route the resulting condition through all existing\n      branch, trap, correction, training and pc_next consumers without\n      changing any arithmetic, dispatch, forwarding or stall protocol.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Update packed ID/EX field extraction for the added fragment bits\n      while retaining every architectural assertion. Cover all six\n      conditions, first differences in each byte, equal operands, signed\n      extrema and opposite signs. Exercise ALU/load/MUL/DIV-to-branch\n      forwarding, x0, held dmem, unready imem, skid consumption, redirect\n      kills and taken versus untaken misaligned targets. Check exact RVFI\n      operands/PC/traps/order, unchanged ready-bus resolution/retirement\n      cycles and exactly-once predictor training and memory side effects.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
