{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category') == 'structural' or d['id'] in ['hyp-20261004-001-r5s0','hyp-20261004-002-r5s1']:\n  print('\\\\nID',d['id'],d.get('title'),d.get('outcome'))\n  print('METRICS',json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ['fitness','delta_pct','fmax_mhz','cycles','lut4','ff','critical_path','error']}))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis')\n  print('PROPOSAL',h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID hyp-20261004-002-r1s1 Replace combinational division with a bounded multicycle execute unit improvement\nMETRICS {\"fitness\": 82.05, \"delta_pct\": 576.98, \"fmax_mhz\": 36.852, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"lut4\": 3150, \"ff\": 600, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_1_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_q_14_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -24.323, \"arrival_ns\": 34.618, \"logic_cells\": 56, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_rf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"]}, \"error\": null}\nPROPOSAL Give DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU a shared, blocking multicycle execution\nunit, leaving the base integer ALU and existing multiplication datapaths\non their current single-cycle path. Remove all synthesizable / and %\nlogic from the core's instantiated ALU. The divider captures the actual\nforwarded source values once and computes unsigned magnitudes using\nfour explicitly unrolled restoring binary division steps per clock,\nwith quotient and remainder registered between groups. Eight groups\nproduce all 32 quotient bits. Capture operand magnitudes and sign flags\non the launch edge, and apply sign correction to the eighth group's\noutput when registering the completed result; do not add separate\npreparation or sign-correction states. This is four binary steps per\ncycle, not a large\ntable of trial multiples. Share the quotient/remainder state across all\nfour operations, use a widened trial remainder and subtraction borrow\nto choose each quotient bit, and register the completed signed result\nbefore it enters the normal EX/MEM result and bypass network.\n\nHold the divide instruction and younger work while the unit is busy,\nbut let older EX/MEM and MEM/WB instructions drain. Emit an invalid\nEX/MEM bubble once the older instruction advances; never retain and\nreissue an older store merely because the divider is busy. Keep data\nbus stalls distinct from divider stalls, preserve older WB values needed\nby a held instruction, suppress redirects from invalid entries, and\naccept the divider result into EX/MEM exactly once when MEM can advance.\nHold a completed resul\n…[25656 of 28728 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d0c9b0a91cd5172c]…\n MHz, with 3775 logic cells,\n804 registers and two DSPs. Projected fitness is 131.73 iter/sec,\nabout 4.81 percent above 125.68. The new worst path is inside the\nunchanged divider rather than forwarding into the ordinary ALU.\n\nExpect five percent higher fitness with medium confidence. The margin\nabove the 4.6-percent acceptance threshold is narrow: unchanged cycles\nrequire median Fmax above about 62.76 MHz. Reproduce the specified\nbypass structure and measure the actual Gowin median; implementations\nwith duplicate WB/early-MEM muxes reached only 61.152 MHz. Full formal\nand trace cosim remain implementation-stage gates, not claims of this\nprototype. The main risks are the ALU-to-operand feedback path, early\ndivider operand timing and physical routing. Preserve nret=1, all external ports,\nRVFI order/operands/traps, decoder default illegality, exact ALTOPS\nformulas, real RV32M arithmetic and the unchanged liveness bound.\nUse the unchanged formal, cosim, CoreMark CRC/marker/UART and FPGA\nevaluation gates.\n\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
