mpute its top magnitude\nnibble as ~raw_a[31:28] + (raw_a[27:0]==0), modulo 16.\nDetect D>=16 directly from raw b: for a negative signed operand it is\n!(&raw_b[31:4]) || raw_b[3:0]==0; otherwise it is |raw_b[31:4].\n\nPrepare and register all divisor multiples M[k]=k*abs(b), k=1..15,\nat explicitly unsigned 36-bit width in this same first busy clock.\nDo not put a conditional magnitude adder followed by multiple\nadders in series. Let neg_b be the captured signed-negative flag and\nV=zero_extend_36(raw_b XOR {32{neg_b}}), so abs(b)=V+neg_b.\nCompute each odd multiple directly \n…[12685 of 15757 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c6867577306cbff9]…\nogic cells and 1076 registers, versus champion 4592\nand 1073, with unchanged 40 LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. The\nmedian-placement worst path is now ALU-to-memory at 16.189 ns.\nThese are prototype measurements, not an orchestrator acceptance result.\nFull formal remains an implementation gate and is not claimed here.\nScratch sources and artifacts are evidence only, never build dependencies.\n\nThis projects approximately 192.27 iterations/sec, a 10.17 percent gain\nover 174.53. Expect ten percent with medium confidence: the slower\nplacement-zero result and competing divider/branch paths show mapping\nsensitivity. Acceptance requires more than 182.558 iterations/sec,\napproximately 87.154 MHz at unchanged cycles. Require the unchanged\nformal, arithmetic, trace cosim, canonical CoreMark validation and\nmedian vendor fitness gates. Keep nret=1, every external memory/RVFI\nport, captured operands, traps, strict order, bounded progress, arbitrary\nbus backpressure and all evaluation invariants without modification.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
