{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'predictor|predict|return.address|jalr|gshare|bimodal' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Replace combinational division with a bounded multicycle execute unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench result has median Fmax 5.442 MHz, 12312 LUT4s,\\nand a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nalu.sv currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and remainder\\nas full combinational / and % expressions selected into the common EX\\nresult. This is a strong candidate for the extreme arithmetic depth:\\neven ordinary instructions must meet the timing of this shared result\\npath. The experiment log has no earlier structural attempts, and no\\nLESSONS.md exists. Trading a few extra cycles on DIV/REM for a much shorter\\nclock period should improve CoreMark iterations per second substantially.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench result has median Fmax 5.442 MHz, 12312 LUT4s,\\nand a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nalu.sv currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and remainder\\nas full combinational / and % expressions selected into the common EX\\nresult. This is a strong candidate for the extreme arithmetic depth:\\neven ordinary instructions must meet the timing of this shared result\\npath. The experiment log has no earlier structural attempts, and no\\nLESSONS.md exists. Trading a few extra cycles on DIV/REM for a much shorter\\nclock period should improve CoreMark iterations per second substantially.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Give DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU a shared, blocking multicycle execution\\nunit, leaving the base integer ALU and existing multiplication datapaths\\non their current single-cycle path. Remove all synthesizable / and %\\nlogic from the core's instantiated ALU. The divider captures the actual\\nforwarded source values once and computes unsigned magnitudes using\\nfour explicitly unrolled restoring binary division steps per clock,\\nwith quotient and remainder registered between groups. Eight groups\\nproduce all 32 quotient bits. Capture ope\n…[237964 of 241036 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d46c6d455e002365]…\noperands/PCs/orders and exactly-once memory effects. Check that\\nregistered recovery_pc stays equal to the complementary successor\\nand independent of live branch operands throughout EX holds; verify\\nthe existing ready-bus liveness bound and real load-use interlocks.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 204.02, \"delta_pct\": 6.11, \"vs_baseline\": 1583.33, \"fmax_mhz\": 91.231, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4471643, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4915, \"ff\": 1257, \"seeds\": [80.649, 91.231, 91.231], \"perturbations\": [[0, 80.649, 10], [1, 91.231, 12], [2, 91.231, 12]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_23_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -7.399, \"arrival_ns\": 17.694, \"logic_cells\": 10, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 10, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T18:53:24.937497Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
