{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/LESSONS.md')\nprint('LESSONS.md:', p.read_text() if p.exists() else 'absent')\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'])\n  print({k:d.get(k) for k in ('outcome','fitness','delta_pct','fmax_mhz','cycles','critical_path','error')})\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict):\n   print('MOTIVATION:',h.get('motivation',''))\n   print('HYPOTHESIS:',h.get('hypothesis',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "LESSONS.md: absent\n\n hyp-20261004-003-r1s2 Fetch-stage bimodal prediction with direct branch targets\n{'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 12.78, 'delta_pct': 5.45, 'fmax_mhz': 5.37, 'cycles': 4201766, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_2_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -187.322, 'arrival_ns': 197.617, 'logic_cells': 153, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}, 'error': None}\nMOTIVATION: This core has no registered IF/ID stage: the instruction at the fetch PC\nis decoded directly into ID/EX. Nevertheless, every taken conditional\nbranch and every JAL/JALR currently redirects in EX and discards the\nyounger fetch, even when the destination is predictable. CoreMark's\nrepeated loops and direct calls provide opportunities to eliminate\nthese bubbles under the same approximately 22% instruction/data stalls.\nThe only recorded experiment is the baseline; there are no previous\npredictor attempts or LESSONS.md entries. Its 199.837 ns worst path runs\nthrough forwarding and the combinational M-extension ALU, so a small\nfetch predictor has plausible timing headroom, although routing must\nstill be measured with Gowin.\n\nA read-only run of the existing CoreMark ELF through the unmodified\nreference ISS counted 2,922,015 instructions between its MMIO markers,\nincluding 529,588 conditional branches (294,425 taken), 49,367 JALs,\nand 13,735 JALRs, with no traps or out-of-bounds accesses. A sequential\ntwo-bit direction model with 64 entries produced 51,857 conditional\nnext-PC misses, versus 111,175 direction misses for static backward-taken\nprediction. Removing direct-JAL corrections as well gives 291,935 net\ncorrections saved. Against the recorded 4,491,485 baseline cycles,\na one-cycle-per-correction model projects 6.95% throughput improvement\nat unchanged Fmax. This is an estimate, not an RTL/stall simulation or\ntiming result. A 256-entry model only raised that estimate to 7.15%,\nso the smaller 64-entry table is the proposed implementation.\n\nHYPOTHESIS: Add one lightwei\n…[59271 of 62343 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:33c7ba64e5283c9c]…\nn during subsequent pipeline holds.\nReset pending validity and all counter state deterministically.\nPreserve registered-only multiplier/divider dispatch, captured operands,\nresult handshakes, EX/MEM drain behavior and retirement-gap bounds.\n\nAt the established 4,471,643 cycles, exceeding the champion by 4.6 percent\nrequires median Gowin Fmax above 89.931 MHz. Matching the champion's\n91.79 MHz would score about 205.27 iter/sec, a 6.76 percent improvement.\nProject seven percent with medium confidence; this candidate is not\nmeasured. The primary risk is that synthesis shares the recovery and\narchitectural pc_next muxes or the fetch prediction adder becomes the\nnext limit. Keep recovery_pc as independently captured metadata and\ninspect the vendor timing path for the intended branch-outcome boundary.\nPreserve nret=1, all IO/RVFI fields, exact order, default-illegal decoder\ndiscipline, full-width trap/target semantics, memory bounds, real RV32M\nand ALTOPS behavior, and every unchanged correctness/evaluation gate.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
