{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print(d['id'],d['title'],d.get('fitness'),d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('cycles'),d.get('outcome'))\nfor p in [Path('Makefile'),Path('test/cosim/reference.py')]:\n print('\\\\nFILE',p)\n print(p.read_text()[:17000] if p.name=='reference.py' else p.read_text())\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-003-r1s2 Fetch-stage bimodal prediction with direct branch targets 12.78 5.37 4201766 regression\nhyp-20261004-003-r2s2 Tagged cached-target prediction on the multicycle-divider champion 94.67 39.69 4192580 regression\nhyp-20261004-003-r3s2 Timing-isolated bimodal prediction with one-bit EX recovery 104.19 43.779 4201740 regression\nhyp-20261004-003-r4s2 Compact registered lookahead prediction without recovery feedback 113.4 47.694 4205657 regression\nhyp-20261004-003-r5s2 Compact bimodal prediction with word-address target arithmetic 131.29 58.887 4485269 regression\nhyp-20261004-003-r6s2 Folded-PC agree prediction with timing-isolated training 139.53 62.392 4471643 regression\nhyp-20261004-003-r7s2 Agree prediction with registered direct recovery targets 169.26 75.685 4471643 regression\nhyp-20261004-003-r8s2 Agree prediction behind the registered arithmetic boundary 189.3 84.648 4471643 regression\nhyp-20261004-003-r9s2 Agree prediction with recovery isolated from decode operand capture 200.29 89.562 4471643 regression\nhyp-20261004-003-r10s2 Agree prediction with recovery address selected before branch resolution 204.02 91.231 4471643 improvement\n\nFILE Makefile\n.PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\n# Resolve OSS CAD Suite path so commands work even when the user hasn't\n# sourced .toolchain/oss-cad-suite/environment in this shell.\nTOOLCHAIN_DIR := $(CURDIR)/.toolchain\nOSS_BIN       := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/oss-cad-suite/bin\nLOCAL_BIN     := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/bin\nexport PATH := $(OSS_BIN):$(LOCAL_BIN):$(PATH)\n\n# Orchestrator knobs (pass-through to tools.orchestrator):\n#   N        — number of rounds for `make loop` (default 10).\n#   K        — tournament size, slots per round (default 1 = sequential).\n#   AGENT    — codex (default) or claude. Honors a pre-existing\n#              AGENT_PROVIDER env var if AGENT isn't set on the make\n#              command line.\n#   BASE     — when forking a new TARGET, copy from cores/<BASE>/.\n#              \n…[19241 of 22313 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:57f520189631996e]…\nap_kwargs, wrd=rd, wval=(pc + 4) & MASK)\n\n        if op == 0x37:  # LUI\n            return self._retire(**trap_kwargs, wrd=rd, wval=imm_u & MASK)\n\n        if op == 0x17:  # AUIPC\n            return self._retire(**trap_kwargs, wrd=rd, wval=(pc + imm_u) & MASK)\n\n        if op == 0x0F:  # MISC-MEM (FENCE / FENCE.I) — architectural NOP\n            return self._retire(**trap_kwargs)\n\n        if op == 0x73:  # SYSTEM\n            if instr == 0x00100073:\n                return self._retire(**trap_kwargs)\n            return self._retire(**trap_kwargs, trap=1)\n\n        # Unknown opcode (AMO 0x2F, etc.) — DUT decoder default-illegal.\n        return self._retire(**trap_kwargs, trap=1)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    cpu = RV32IM()\n    cpu.load_elf(sys.argv[1])\n    max_insns = int(sys.argv[2]) if len(sys.argv) > 2 else 10_000_000\n    import json\n    for _ in range(max_insns):\n        r = cpu.step()\n        if r is None:\n            break\n        print(json.dumps(r))\n        if r['insn'] == 0x00100073:\n            break\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
