{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|prediction|return.address|return stack|gshare|BTB|JALR|agree' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Replace combinational division with a bounded multicycle execute unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench result has median Fmax 5.442 MHz, 12312 LUT4s,\\nand a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nalu.sv currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and remainder\\nas full combinational / and % expressions selected into the common EX\\nresult. This is a strong candidate for the extreme arithmetic depth:\\neven ordinary instructions must meet the timing of this shared result\\npath. The experiment log has no earlier structural attempts, and no\\nLESSONS.md exists. Trading a few extra cycles on DIV/REM for a much shorter\\nclock period should improve CoreMark iterations per second substantially.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench result has median Fmax 5.442 MHz, 12312 LUT4s,\\nand a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nalu.sv currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and remainder\\nas full combinational / and % expressions selected into the common EX\\nresult. This is a strong candidate for the extreme arithmetic depth:\\neven ordinary instructions must meet the timing of this shared result\\npath. The experiment log has no earlier structural attempts, and no\\nLESSONS.md exists. Trading a few extra cycles on DIV/REM for a much shorter\\nclock period should improve CoreMark iterations per second substantially.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Give DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU a shared, blocking multicycle execution\\nunit, leaving the base integer ALU and existing multiplication datapaths\\non their current single-cycle path. Remove all synthesizable / and %\\nlogic from the core's instantiated ALU. The divider captures the actual\\nforwarded source values once and computes unsigned magnitudes using\\nfour explicitly unrolled restoring binary division steps per clock,\\nwith quotient and remainder registered between groups. Eight groups\\nproduce all 32 quotient bits. Capture ope\n…[276766 of 279838 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:74e48032562293e4]…\nct RVFI operands,\\nPC/order/traps, one producer retirement, no wrong memory request or\\narithmetic launch, exact MEM fallback and bounded ready-bus progress.\\nInclude both new RTL modules in the pipeline test source list and\\nadapt bundle unpacking without weakening any architectural assertion.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 182.8, \"delta_pct\": -10.4, \"vs_baseline\": 1408.25, \"fmax_mhz\": 81.761, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4472807, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5210, \"ff\": 1296, \"seeds\": [81.539, 81.761, 81.761], \"perturbations\": [[0, 81.539, 15], [1, 81.761, 15], [2, 81.761, 15]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_q_31_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_1_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -7.264, \"arrival_ns\": 17.558, \"logic_cells\": 21, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T20:03:42.268188Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/LESSONS.md')\nprint('LESSONS:', p.read_text() if p.exists() else 'Absent')\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n print(r['id'],r.get('category'),r.get('title'), 'fitness',r.get('fitness'),'cycles',r.get('cycles'),'MHz',r.get('fmax_mhz'),'outcome',r.get('outcome'))\n if r.get('category')=='predictor':\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict):\n   print('MOTIVATION:',h.get('motivation',''))\n   print('PROPOSAL:',h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  else: print('PROPOSAL:',h)\n  print('NOTES:',r.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/LESSONS.md')\nprint('LESSONS:', p.read_text() if p.exists() else 'Absent')\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n print(r['id'],r.get('category'),r.get('title'), 'fitness',r.get('fitness'),'cycles',r.get('cycles'),'MHz',r.get('fmax_mhz'),'outcome',r.get('outcome'))\n if r.get('category')=='predictor':\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict):\n   print('MOTIVATION:',h.get('motivation',''))\n   print('PROPOSAL:',h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  else: print('PROPOSAL:',h)\n  print('NOTES:',r.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "LESSONS: Absent\nbaseline-bench-0e2f75b micro_opt Baseline retest for cores/bench fitness 12.12 cycles 4491485 MHz 5.442 outcome improvement\nhyp-20261004-001-r1s0 micro_opt Shorten combinational division with a shared radix-4 datapath fitness 13.01 cycles 4491485 MHz 5.844 outcome regression\nhyp-20261004-002-r1s1 structural Replace combinational division with a bounded multicycle execute unit fitness 82.05 cycles 4491485 MHz 36.852 outcome improvement\nhyp-20261004-003-r1s2 predictor Fetch-stage bimodal prediction with direct branch targets fitness 12.78 cycles 4201766 MHz 5.37 outcome regression\nMOTIVATION: This core has no registered IF/ID stage: the instruction at the fetch PC\nis decoded directly into ID/EX. Nevertheless, every taken conditional\nbranch and every JAL/JALR currently redirects in EX and discards the\nyounger fetch, even when the destination is predictable. CoreMark's\nrepeated loops and direct calls provide opportunities to eliminate\nthese bubbles under the same approximately 22% instruction/data stalls.\nThe only recorded experiment is the baseline; there are no previous\npredictor attempts or LESSONS.md entries. Its 199.837 ns worst path runs\nthrough forwarding and the combinational M-extension ALU, so a small\nfetch predictor has plausible timing headroom, although routing must\nstill be measured with Gowin.\n\nA read-only run of the existing CoreMark ELF through the unmodified\nreference ISS counted 2,922,015 instructions between its MMIO markers,\nincluding 529,588 conditional branches (294,425 taken), 49,367 JALs,\nand 13,735 JALRs, with no traps or out-of-bounds accesses. A sequential\ntwo-bit direction model with 64 entries produced 51,857 conditional\nnext-PC misses, versus 111,175 direction misses for static backward-taken\nprediction. Removing direct-JAL corrections as well gives 291,935 net\ncorrections saved. Against the recorded 4,491,485 baseline cycles,\na one-cycle-per-correction model projects 6.95% throughput improvement\nat unchanged Fmax. This is an estimate, not an RTL/stall simulation or\ntimi\n…[67504 of 70576 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c4187b38c57eebe3]…\nipline, traps and full-width addresses, real RV32M and ALTOPS behavior,\nmemory bounds, and every unchanged formal/cosim/CoreMark validation gate.\nThis is a single carry-prediction hypothesis; add no load-value predictor,\ncache, fetch queue, branch-table redesign or arithmetic latency change.\n\nProject nine percent higher fitness with medium confidence, primarily\nfrom a shorter Gowin critical forwarding path. The trace model predicts\nnegligible added cycles, but actual stalls and queued training may change\nits count. With 1,371 added cycles, acceptance requires median Fmax above\napproximately 95.456 MHz; a ten-percent clock improvement would yield\nabout 224.35 iter/sec. Neither is a measurement of the proposed RTL.\nThe main risks are the new carry-validation control path becoming critical,\nsynthesis reconnecting the full exact adder to speculative forwarding,\nand the unchanged exact memory-address path limiting further Fmax. Check\nthe vendor timing report and measured marker-bracketed cycles together.\n\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
