{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category') == 'predictor' and d.get('round_id',0) in range(5,12):\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('RESULT',d.get('fitness'),d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('cycles'))\n  print('NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes','')[-2200:])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-003-r5s2 Compact bimodal prediction with word-address target arithmetic\nAdd one compact 32-entry, two-bit bimodal direction predictor indexed\nby fetch PC[6:2], with unconditional direct-JAL prediction. Reset the\ncounters to weakly not taken (01). Use explicit clocked counter bits,\none asynchronous fetch-direction read, and old-state reads for\nsaturating updates. Do not add registered lookahead, a BTB, tags,\ncached targets, global history, a return stack, or a pipeline stage.\nThe single architectural angle is eliminating recurring control\nbubbles with minimal predictor logic on the current multiplier-isolated\nchampion; all existing arithmetic datapaths stay intact.\n\nPositively predecode legal conditional BRANCH funct3 values and JAL\nfrom raw imem_data. Derive their exact B/J displacement, but implement\nthe prediction target as one 19-bit WORD-address addition, rather\nthan a 32-bit byte-address adder followed by a wide range comparison.\nAdmit only source PCs with PC[31:20]==0 and PC[1:0]==0, and only\ndisplacements with bit 1 zero. Form target_word modulo 2^19 as\n{1'b0, PC[19:2]} plus the signed B/J displacement divided by four,\nsign-extended to 19 bits. Require target_word[18]==0 and reconstruct\n{12'b0, target_word[17:0], 2'b00}. For an admitted source, the JAL\ndisplacement bounds place the mathematical sum in [-2^18, 2^19),\nso the high bit rejects both negative and >=1-MiB targets without\nany unsafe modular alias. This also covers the narrower B displacement.\nRejecting a candidate must select ordinary PC+4, leaving architectural\ntarget calculation and misalignment traps in EX authoritative. Keep\nthe existing full-width sequential PC+4 and EX recovery arithmetic;\nthe shortening applies only to speculative B/J target generation.\n\nSelect the admitted target for conditional branches when the indexed\ncounter MSB is one, and for JAL unconditionally. Keep JALR sequential.\nPrediction and direction lookup depend only on the registered fetch\nPC, raw instruction and stored predictor state. There is no EX-update\n\n…[32218 of 35290 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b93fe5e103849cba]…\nh addresses, real RV32M and ALTOPS behavior,\nmemory bounds, and every unchanged formal/cosim/CoreMark validation gate.\nThis is a single carry-prediction hypothesis; add no load-value predictor,\ncache, fetch queue, branch-table redesign or arithmetic latency change.\n\nProject nine percent higher fitness with medium confidence, primarily\nfrom a shorter Gowin critical forwarding path. The trace model predicts\nnegligible added cycles, but actual stalls and queued training may change\nits count. With 1,371 added cycles, acceptance requires median Fmax above\napproximately 95.456 MHz; a ten-percent clock improvement would yield\nabout 224.35 iter/sec. Neither is a measurement of the proposed RTL.\nThe main risks are the new carry-validation control path becoming critical,\nsynthesis reconnecting the full exact adder to speculative forwarding,\nand the unchanged exact memory-address path limiting further Fmax. Check\nthe vendor timing report and measured marker-bracketed cycles together.\n\nRESULT 182.8 81.761 4472807\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
