{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; git diff --check; sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r7s2.yaml; command -v riscv32-unknown-elf-gcc; command -v verilator; rg -n 'ignore|hypotheses|expected_impact|validate' tools/agents/hypothesis.py tools/sandbox.py .gitignore\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-003-r7s2\ntitle: \"Agree prediction with registered direct recovery targets\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion scores 154.12 iter/sec at 73.574 MHz and needs\n  4,773,913 cycles for the canonical ten-iteration CoreMark run.\n  LESSONS.md is absent. Six previous predictor experiments passed\n  correctness but lost their tournament rounds: recurring control\n  bubbles were removed, while their clock rates failed to beat the\n  arithmetic improvements competing in those rounds. The last agree\n  predictor needed 4,471,643 cycles, but ran on the previous divider.\n  The current champion's reported path still crosses EX, IF and early\n  divider launch. Adding prediction without shortening that recovery\n  path leaves only about two percent clock margin for acceptance.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one compact direct-control predictor whose recovery targets are\n  prepared before the existing ID/EX register. Use 64 two-bit agree\n  counters indexed by PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], reset to weak agreement (10).\n  For positively validated conditional branches, use instruction[31]\n  as backward-taken/forward-not-taken bias, selecting that bias when\n  the counter MSB predicts agreement and its inverse otherwise.\n  Predict legal JAL unconditionally; keep JALR sequential. This is a\n  predictor-only change, preserving the current arithmetic units,\n  forwarded-operand capture, retirement width and pipeline stages.\n\n  Compute the exact full-width PC+B/J-immediate target and PC+4 from\n  the raw fetch PC/instruction before ID/EX. Share the direct-target\n  calculation between the fetch next-PC choice and the target carried\n  with that instruction; do not recompute the direct branch/JAL target\n  from registered PC and immediate in EX. Capture direct_target,\n  fallthrough_pc and one predicted_transfer bit in ID/EX, holding and\n  flushing them with the complete instruction. These are prepared\n  recovery addresses, not a cached target table. Keep full RV32 modular\n  target arithmetic; never substitute a truncated or range-cla\n…[9975 of 13047 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cb9b0a80863de802]…\nrcase `low`/`medium`/`high`.\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:388:    We deliberately do NOT coerce `expected_impact` or any other field —\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:438:    hyp_dir = hypotheses_dir(target)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:457:    (default: any YAML in experiments/hypotheses/), revert those changes\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:475:                         YAMLs to cores/<target>/experiments/hypotheses/.\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:487:    # Stream agent output to cores/<target>/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.{hyp_id}.log\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:492:    # log. The per-slot path is gitignored by the `.agent.*.log` /\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:494:    hyp_dir = hypotheses_dir(target)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:496:    # Codex needs an output-last-message file; claude ignores it.\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:514:    ws_hyp_dir = ws / \"cores\" / target / \"experiments\" / \"hypotheses\"\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:557:                                  lambda p: p.startswith(f\"cores/{target}/experiments/hypotheses/\"))\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
