{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"The first carry-select layout also loses Fmax because byte-sum generation remains in EX. I’m testing a different placement: capture the independent byte sums at ID/EX, then finish exact carry selection in EX. This keeps instruction latency unchanged and moves the arithmetic off the branch-to-fetch path."}}
