{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r15s1.yaml')\ns=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('title: \\\"Share an exact byte carry-select lane between ALU and branch ordering\\\"','title: \\\"Retime exact arithmetic into ID byte sums and EX carry selection\\\"')\ns=s.replace('  One exact shared arithmetic lane can shorten these paths without any\\\\n  speculative value, recovery protocol or extra instruction latency.','  Retiming an exact shared arithmetic lane across ID/EX can shorten both\\\\n  paths without speculative values or extra instruction latency. An\\\\n  EX-only byte carry-select prototype was slower, so placement of the\\\\n  byte arithmetic before the existing register is essential.')\ns=s.replace('  behind the existing ID/EX registers. Share that physical lane between','  split across the existing ID/EX registers. Compute independent byte\\\\n  sum alternatives in ID, capture them together, and finish exact carry\\\\n  selection in EX. Share this physical lane between')\ns=s.replace('  For registered operands A and B, form Y=B XOR replicated subtract-mode\\\\n  and incoming carry c0=subtract-mode. Split A and Y into four bytes.','  From the fully resolved decode ALU operands A and B, form Y=B XOR\\\\n  replicated subtract-mode and incoming carry c0=subtract-mode. Split\\\\n  A and Y into four bytes. All preparatory arithmetic is in ID, after\\\\n  the existing source forwarding and immediate/AUIPC operand selection.')\ns=s.replace('  Compute G[k]=S0[k][8] and P[k]=AND-reduction(Abyte XOR Ybyte).\\\\n  Derive actual incoming carries and final carry with a balanced group','  Compute P[k]=AND-reduction(Abyte XOR Ybyte). Capture both complete\\\\n  four-by-nine-bit sum vectors, the four propagate bits, equality,\\\\n  operand-sign difference and A sign in ID/EX with the instruction.\\\\n  G[k] is the saved S0[k][8], so it needs no duplicate register. Hold\\\\n  these fields under every existing payload stall and reset them with\\\\n  the payload; do not let flush select a wide zero-valued arithmetic\\\\n  payload. Existing validity/control bubbles still suppress all effects.\\\\n  In EX derive actual incoming carries and final carry with a balanced group')\ns=s.replace('  Expose equality from a balanced reduction of A XOR B independently\\\\n  of carry. In subtract mode, unsigned A<B is NOT c4; signed A<B is\\\\n  A[31] when operand signs differ and unsigned-less otherwise. Consume','  Compute equality in ID from a balanced reduction of A XOR B and save\\\\n  it independently of carry. In EX subtract mode, unsigned A<B is NOT\\\\n  c4; signed A<B is saved A sign when saved operand signs differ and\\\\n  unsigned-less otherwise. Consume')\ns=s.replace('  limit timing. Check Gowin mapping and score measured median Fmax times','  limit timing. The dependent recurrence is now EX prefix/select,\\\\n  decode operand forwarding/selection, then one local byte sum; there\\\\n  must be no new full-width carry computation before the ID/EX register.\\\\n  Check Gowin mapping and score measured median Fmax times')\ns=s.replace('      Add an exact shared ADD/SUB lane with four unsigned byte sum pairs,\\\\n      block generate/propagate and balanced exact carry-prefix selection,\\\\n      independent equality and subtract-mode ordering flags. Use explicit\\\\n      widths; infer no clock, prediction, replay or long fallback.','      Define exact byte-sum preparation and EX carry-selection logic,\\\\n      with an explicit existing-register boundary between them. Finish\\\\n      from saved nine-bit sum pairs, propagate bits, mode and comparison\\\\n      metadata; infer no prediction, replay or full-width fallback.')\ns=s.replace('      Add one instruction-only subtract-mode bit to ID/EX, preserving\\\\n      architectural operands and all retirement metadata.','      Extend ID/EX with two packed 36-bit byte-sum vectors, four propagate\\\\n      bits, equality/sign metadata and subtract mode. Preserve architectural\\\\n      operands and retirement metadata; saved sum carry bits supply G.')\ns=s.replace('      Capture arithmetic mode from validated ALU operation/branch controls\\\\n      alongside final ALU inputs; preserve reset, stall holds, flush/control\\\\n      bubbles and existing operand acquisition.','      Prepare all independent nine-bit sum pairs and comparison metadata\\\\n      from fully forwarded, selected decode inputs and validated mode.\\\\n      Capture them with the existing ID/EX payload and preserve reset,\\\\n      hold, flush/control-bubble and operand-acquisition behavior.')\ns=s.replace('      Instantiate the exact arithmetic lane, route ADD/SUB and SLT/SLTU\\\\n      through it and expose equality/ordering flags to EX. Remove duplicate\\\\n      native arithmetic/relational arms and preserve all other operations.','      Finish exact arithmetic from the captured partial sums and mode,\\\\n      route ADD/SUB and SLT/SLTU through it, and expose saved equality and\\\\n      exact ordering to EX. Remove duplicate native arithmetic/relational\\\\n      arms; preserve all other operations from their original operands.')\ns=s.replace('      Drive the shared lane from captured mode and registered ALU inputs.','      Drive the shared lane from captured sum vectors, propagate/mode\\\\n      and comparison metadata.')\ns=s.replace('      Check hardware sums and subtract-mode comparisons against an\\\\n      independent reference. Cover all byte-boundary carries/borrows,','      Check real preparation and completion arithmetic against an\\\\n      independent full-width reference, including saved payload stability\\\\n      during holds. Cover all byte-boundary carries/borrows,')\np.write_text(s)\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nd=yaml.safe_load(s);jsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()));print('VALID',d['title'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
